No licence is granted for this work. Absent a separate written agreement, no
permission is given to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute,
sublicense or sell it, in whole or in part.

This is a deliberate placeholder, not an intended end state. The choice
between a permissive licence and a copyleft one is being deferred, because it
is entangled with an unresolved question about a vendored dependency — see
`apps/web/vendor/min2phase.PROVENANCE.md`. Reserving all rights does not
settle that question: distributing a GPL-licensed component from an
all-rights-reserved repository is no more permitted than from a permissive
one, so min2phase still has to be replaced before any release. The plan is
`dev-docs/two-phase-plan.md`.

Third-party components retain their own licences. Vendored artifacts under
`apps/web/vendor/` are generated from pinned dependencies rather than
committed, and are governed by those dependencies' terms.
